      "source_citation": "Khattab, I.S., Bandarkar, F., Khoubnasabjafari, M., Jouyban, A. (2012). Density, viscosity, surface tension, and molar volume of propylene glycol + water mixtures from 293 to 323 K and correlations by the Jouyban-Acree model. Arabian J. Chem. 10(Suppl. 1), S71-S75. Measured density at 293 K, propylene glycol mole fraction x1 = 0.141 (= 40.94 wt%): 1.0312 g/cm3 = 1031.2 kg/m3. This measured dataset is independent of the Melinder correlation that the CoolProp model is fitted to, so the check is a genuine cross-validation rather than a circular one.",
